{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-05fef638-f3b3-4305-9ad4-1bdebb35bb12","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b33885e150de4dc1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-t93iw4co/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E001.md","content":"# RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support and deployment mechanism investigation\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's strategic dependency: whether RHCL (Kuadrant: Authorino + Limitador) is officially supported on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS), and which of three bounded deployment mechanisms is viable for MaaS authentication and rate limiting on xKS. The outcome selects one of three conditional branches for deploying Kuadrant on xKS and gates the MaaS deployment validation work. The strategy flags this as \"Unknown — needs immediate validation with the OpenShift team\" and a Sprint 1 priority.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Engage the OpenShift RHCL team to confirm official xKS support commitment and timeline; escalate to product leadership if no commitment is obtained (per the strategy's Sprint 1 directive).\n- Determine whether official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts exist and are supported for non-OLM, Helm-only xKS installation.\n- Validate that Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) can be installed and can function on a CKS test cluster with the Istio GatewayClass (CoreWeave deploys Istio service mesh).\n- Evaluate the three bounded deployment options in the strategy's priority order: (A) official RHCL Helm charts, (B) standalone Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm, (C) direct Envoy ext_authz integration as contingency.\n- Produce a decision record that selects the deployment mechanism with evidence, and documents what works vs. what breaks for each option considered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written decision record states the RHCL official xKS support status (committed / not committed, with timeline), or documents the escalation outcome if uncommitted.\n- The selected deployment mechanism is demonstrated on a CKS test cluster with Istio: Authorino validates an OIDC JWT identity and Limitador enforces a token rate limit (HTTP 429 on exceeded quota) in a test scenario.\n- The decision record names exactly one of the three bounded outcomes (A/B/C) as the recommended path, with evidence for rejecting the others.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input quoted in the strategy).\n\n## Notes\n\nRisks: the RHCL commitment is an external-team decision that cannot be forced; the strategy directs escalation to product leadership if uncommitted. Kuadrant installability on CKS is separately listed as a strategy risk with the standalone and Envoy fallbacks — both are covered by the bounded outcomes of this investigation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64040,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20b78a95a65165e","agent_id":"a61389ab3fb18a498","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"96d2ae5b-5dd1-4df3-ab16-16b7552ec1c0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:09:51.498Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
