{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-05fef638-f3b3-4305-9ad4-1bdebb35bb12","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-831e72e9f4b097d8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-t93iw4co/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E002.md","content":"# MaaS 3.4 GA baseline changeability investigation\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves three strategy assumptions marked \"Needs validation\" about the MaaS 3.4 GA codebase as the xKS Dev Preview baseline: (1) whether the Tenant CRD is extensible in the 3.4 GA baseline so a configurable OIDC group claim path can be added, or is frozen; (2) whether maas-api can be instrumented with Prometheus metrics without conflicting with the 3.4 GA code freeze, or requires a post-3.4 patch; and (3) whether a stable or RC 3.4 build is available to use as the validation baseline. The answers determine the approach of the maas-controller and maas-api implementation work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the MaaS 3.4 GA repository and release policy to determine whether adding a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD is permitted in the baseline, or whether the CRD is frozen.\n- Assess whether maas-api observability instrumentation (Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint) can be added to the 3.4 baseline or must be delivered as a post-3.4 patch (the strategy allows deferring metrics to P1 in that case).\n- Confirm build availability: identify a stable or RC MaaS 3.4 build artifact (version and date) usable as the xKS validation baseline, or escalate unavailability to the MaaS PM (open question: latest date for a stable build, Summit timeline feasibility).\n- Produce a findings record with a go/fallback determination for each question.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The findings record states, with evidence from the MaaS 3.4 repository and release policy, whether the Tenant CRD `groupClaimPath` addition is possible in the baseline or must fall back to documenting the required claim format.\n- The findings record states whether maas-api metrics instrumentation can land in the baseline or requires a post-3.4 patch (or deferral).\n- A stable or RC MaaS 3.4 build artifact is identified (version/date) as the validation baseline, or the unavailability and its timeline impact is escalated and documented.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (determines code-change vs documentation-fallback approach).\n- Enables HLR [P0]: Observability metrics functional (determines instrumentation approach).\n\n## Notes\n\nThe stable-build timing question is owned by the MaaS PM per the strategy's open questions table; the technical questions are answerable from the MaaS source repository and build artifacts.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64040,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20b78a95a65165e","agent_id":"a61389ab3fb18a498","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"619880a7-0a31-4fdc-a556-cfaeee9d3d23","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:09:59.296Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
