{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d5a0dbee-5b9f-4715-bdc0-06ee9d788650","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-96257691bb8b69c8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-t93iw4co/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E003.md","content":"# maas-controller: configurable OIDC group claim mapping and Helm chart\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes the maas-controller support configurable OIDC group claim mapping so that MaaS subscription tiers can be assigned from external OIDC identity provider group claims (e.g. Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) instead of Kubernetes RBAC groups, and packages the maas-controller for Helm-based installation on non-OpenShift Kubernetes. On xKS, user group claims must be sourced from the OIDC token; today the MaaSSubscription controller maps rate-limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on `auth.identity.groups`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD (default: `auth.identity.groups`) that is passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation, so the claim path is configurable per deployment without further code changes.\n- Keep the change additive and configuration-driven: default behavior on RHOAI must be unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n- Package the maas-controller as a Helm chart with configurable values for gateway class name (not `openshift-default`) and OIDC/group-claim settings, for xKS Helm-only installation (no OLM).\n- If the Tenant CRD is frozen in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline (per the baseline changeability investigation), deliver the documented fallback instead of the CRD change: documentation of the required OIDC group claim format and customer IdP configuration guidance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement (strategy acceptance criterion).\n- With no `groupClaimPath` configured, the controller's CEL predicate generation is unchanged from RHOAI MaaS GA behavior (backwards compatibility).\n- The maas-controller is installable via its Helm chart on a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster with configurable gateway class and OIDC values.\n- If the CRD-frozen fallback applies: a document exists specifying the required OIDC group claim format and the customer IdP configuration steps, accepted by the MaaS team.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n- HLR [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n\n## Risks\n\n- The Tenant CRD may be frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA; the fallback (documented claim format, IdP configuration burden pushed to customers) is defined above and selected by the baseline changeability investigation.\n- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is pending human review per the strategy's prerequisites table.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67205,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20b78a95a65165e","agent_id":"a61389ab3fb18a498","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"008a4d61-9894-49ea-88d9-16c191706854","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:10:28.926Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
