{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-23d71b78-67d3-4c20-9b18-748412c4d562","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94e08e9e5803ec17","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-t93iw4co/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E005.md","content":"# Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts (branch A)\n\n## Description\n\nThis branch epic deploys Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on non-OpenShift Kubernetes using official RHCL Helm charts, the strategy's primary deployment option, selected when the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation confirms official RHCL xKS support with Helm-based distribution. It delivers a functioning authentication and rate-limiting enforcement layer for MaaS on xKS, prioritizing CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service with Istio) per the Staff Engineer Input quoted in the strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Install RHCL/Kuadrant on a CKS test cluster via the official RHCL Helm charts, configured for the Istio GatewayClass.\n- Configure Authorino to use the external OIDC identity source (replacing OpenShift's KubernetesTokenReview) with the customer's OIDC issuer URL and JWKS endpoint, aligned with the MaaS AuthPolicy configuration.\n- Confirm Limitador's TokenRateLimitPolicy functionality on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (no code changes expected — it works on any Kubernetes).\n- Enable structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki.\n- Document the RHCL chart installation and configuration procedure for reuse on AKS (envoy-gateway / azure-application-gateway GatewayClass options).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) is installed via official RHCL Helm charts on a CKS cluster and all pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n- Authorino validates an OIDC JWT against the configured external identity provider and rejects invalid tokens, measured by authenticated and rejected test requests.\n- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n- Structured log entries for authentication decisions and rate limit enforcement are emitted and retrievable from the CKS log aggregation, measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador deployment and enforcement).\n- HLR [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (mechanism realization).\n\n## Gate Conditions\n\nExecuted only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome A (official RHCL Helm charts viable). If outcome A does not hold, this epic is replaced by the standalone Authorino + Limitador deployment branch.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72390,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20b78a95a65165e","agent_id":"a61389ab3fb18a498","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"03a2beed-6baa-4035-b89f-42e84db8fb1b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:11:17.642Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
