l identity provider and rejects invalid tokens, measured by authenticated and rejected test requests.\n- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n- Structured log entries for authentication decisions and rate limit enforcement are emitted and retrievable from the CKS log aggregation, measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador deployment and enforcement).\n- HLR [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (mechanism realization).\n\n## Gate Conditions\n\nExecuted only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome B (no official RHCL xKS support; standalone deployment viable). If standalone deployment also fails on xKS, the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency branch applies.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72390,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20b78a95a65165e","agent_id":"a61389ab3fb18a498","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"c25f7f23-1b62-40f0-9e46-9bddfae44c99","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:11:24.732Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
