er integration, group claim to tier mapping, and API key lifecycle.\n- A published document lists all known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA, incorporating the findings from both platform deployment validations.\n- Both documents are technically reviewed against the implemented MaaS on xKS behavior (review sign-off recorded).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR [P1]: Known limitations documented.\n- HLR [P2]: User identity flow documented for xKS deployments.\n\n## Notes\n\nDocumentation Support is \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's prerequisites table; the docs-authoring routing assumes the Red Hat docs content process is available. Priority is P0 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority `Blocker`).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78613,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20b78a95a65165e","agent_id":"a61389ab3fb18a498","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"414dddb4-61ca-434c-942c-60f44f215248","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:12:42.248Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
