{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be37df58ad34f79f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n3\ttitle: 'maas-controller: configurable OIDC group claim mapping and Helm chart'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD is frozen in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline, replace\n15\t    the CRD/code change with documentation of the required OIDC group claim format\n16\t    and customer IdP configuration guidance.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# maas-controller: configurable OIDC group claim mapping and Helm chart\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic makes the maas-controller support configurable OIDC group claim mapping so that MaaS subscription tiers can be assigned from external OIDC identity provider group claims (e.g. Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims) instead of Kubernetes RBAC groups, and packages the maas-controller for Helm-based installation on non-OpenShift Kubernetes. On xKS, user group claims must be sourced from the OIDC token; today the MaaSSubscription controller maps rate-limiting tiers to user groups via CEL predicates on `auth.identity.groups`.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Add a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD (default: `auth.identity.groups`) that is passed through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate generation, so the claim path is configurable per deployment without further code changes.\n43\t- Keep the change additive and configuration-driven: default behavior on RHOAI must be unchanged (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n44\t- Package the maas-controller as a Helm chart with configurable values for gateway class name (not `openshift-default`) and OIDC/group-claim settings, for xKS Helm-only installation (no OLM).\n45\t- If the Tenant CRD is frozen in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline (per the baseline changeability investigation), deliver the documented fallback instead of the CRD change: documentation of the required OIDC group claim format and customer IdP configuration guidance.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the MaaSSubscription controller correctly maps the user to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement (strategy acceptance criterion).\n50\t- With no `groupClaimPath` configured, the controller's CEL predicate generation is unchanged from RHOAI MaaS GA behavior (backwards compatibility).\n51\t- The maas-controller is installable via its Helm chart on a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster with configurable gateway class and OIDC values.\n52\t- If the CRD-frozen fallback applies: a document exists specifying the required OIDC group claim format and the customer IdP configuration steps, accepted by the MaaS team.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n57\t- HLR [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n58\t\n59\t## Risks\n60\t\n61\t- The Tenant CRD may be frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA; the fallback (documented claim format, IdP configuration burden pushed to customers) is defined above and selected by the baseline changeability investigation.\n62\t- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is pending human review per the strategy's prerequisites table.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db943990d4a737f","agent_id":"ad3dc98f22978d58b","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"2a10101e-3c46-480f-aa4e-11c005d8025d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:14:32.498Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be37df58ad34f79f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
