{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb9b5e4746e4a82e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: Kuadrant on xKS via standalone Authorino + Limitador (branch B)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If standalone Authorino + Limitador also cannot be deployed on\n16\t    xKS, fall back to direct Envoy ext_authz integration (branch C).\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Kuadrant on xKS via standalone Authorino + Limitador (branch B)\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis branch epic deploys Kuadrant's components — Authorino and Limitador — standalone via their upstream Helm charts on non-OpenShift Kubernetes, the strategy's fallback deployment option, selected when the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation finds no official RHCL xKS support commitment or no official RHCL Helm charts. It delivers the same authentication and rate-limiting enforcement layer for MaaS on xKS without RHCL distribution support, prioritizing CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service with Istio).\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Install standalone Authorino and Limitador on a CKS test cluster via upstream Helm charts, configured for the Istio GatewayClass.\n42\t- Configure Authorino to use the external OIDC identity source (replacing OpenShift's KubernetesTokenReview) with the customer's OIDC issuer URL and JWKS endpoint, aligned with the MaaS AuthPolicy configuration.\n43\t- Confirm Limitador's TokenRateLimitPolicy functionality on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (no code changes expected).\n44\t- Enable structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki.\n45\t- Document the unsupported-path implications (no RHCL official support) for product leadership visibility, per the strategy's strategic-dependency risk.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Standalone Authorino and Limitador are installed via Helm on a CKS cluster and all pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n50\t- Authorino validates an OIDC JWT against the configured external identity provider and rejects invalid tokens, measured by authenticated and rejected test requests.\n51\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n52\t- Structured log entries for authentication decisions and rate limit enforcement are emitted and retrievable from the CKS log aggregation, measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador deployment and enforcement).\n57\t- HLR [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (mechanism realization).\n58\t\n59\t## Gate Conditions\n60\t\n61\tExecuted only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome B (no official RHCL xKS support; standalone deployment viable). If standalone deployment also fails on xKS, the direct Envoy ext_authz contingency branch applies.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db943990d4a737f","agent_id":"ad3dc98f22978d58b","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"5acd6f7e-1037-4a7