{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdf7de1a736b88f4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: MaaS Dev Preview deployment validation on CKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: The CKS validation deploys the Kuadrant deployment mechanism\n17\t    selected by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation; if no mechanism is viable,\n18\t    the validation scope is rewritten around the selected contingency or re-scoped\n19\t    with product leadership.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 2\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# MaaS Dev Preview deployment validation on CKS\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis epic deploys the full MaaS Dev Preview stack on CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service) — the priority platform per the Staff Engineer Input quoted in the strategy — using the adapted MaaS components, their Helm charts, and the Kuadrant deployment mechanism selected by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation. It validates core MaaS functionality (subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, API key and OIDC authentication) and documents what works, what breaks, and the engineering delta versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Deploy maas-api, maas-controller, and payload-processing via their Helm charts on a CKS test cluster with the Istio GatewayClass and cert-manager-issued TLS certificates, with external OIDC configuration.\n46\t- Deploy the selected Kuadrant deployment mechanism (per the investigation outcome) alongside the MaaS components.\n47\t- Validate core functionality: subscription/tier management with OIDC group claims (including a non-standard group claim format via configurable claim path), token rate limiting (HTTP 429 on exceeded quota), API key lifecycle (create, use for inference), and OIDC JWT authentication.\n48\t- Validate cert-manager TLS certificate rotation behavior (requests continue without interruption during renewal).\n49\t- Confirm CKS Prometheus scrape targets and Grafana Loki log aggregation are accessible for the MaaS observability work (strategy assumption \"Needs validation\").\n50\t- Record what works vs. what breaks and the engineering delta (code changes, configuration changes, Helm chart packaging), feeding the known-limitations documentation.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given a CKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API (Istio) installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n55\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n56\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and the configurable claim path set to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the user is mapped to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n57\t- Given cert-manager-issued TLS certificates are rotated, then active inference requests continue without interruption and new requests succeed with the new certificate, measured by zero connection errors during the rotation window and successful TLS handshake validation post-rotation.\n58\t- A validation report exists documenting what works, what breaks, and the engineering delta for MaaS on CKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA, including confirmation (or refutation) of CKS Prometheus/Loki accessibility.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on CKS.\n63\t- HLR [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (validation).\n64\t- HLR [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (validation).\n65\t- HLR [P0]: API key authentication (`sk-oai-*` flow) functional on xKS (validation).\n66\t- HLR [P1]: Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (validation).\n67\t\n68\t## Risks\n69\t\n70\t- MaaS 3.4 GA stable build timing is an external schedule constraint (Summit May 2026); mitigations per the strategy: obtain the RC build by April 27, run CKS validation in parallel with RC testing, and maintain a RHOAI 3.3 MaaS fallback demo. Externally controlled timing is tracked here as a risk, not as an acceptance criterion.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db943990d4a737f","agent_id":"ad3dc98f22978d58b","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"8acb456c-610b-4c68-b5a9-7a72ceb96726","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:14:41.634Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdf7de1a736b88f4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
