d logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n46\t- Given a user exceeding a configured rate limit, when the enforcement decision is made, then a structured log entry for the rate limit enforcement (429 response, exceeded quota) is retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki, measured by querying with label filters.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR [P1]: Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input).\n51\t\n52\t## Notes\n53\t\n54\tJoint ownership with the xKS Platform team per the strategy's affected components table (\"MaaS / xKS Platform\"); the xKS Platform team contributes the CKS Loki integration. Authorino/Limitador structured logging configuration is guided by the RHCL/OpenShift team per the impacted teams table.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db943990d4a737f","agent_id":"ad3dc98f22978d58b","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"5c53c219-37d8-44fc-89d8-6453389161b4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:14:46.735Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa94a098fab7d7fd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
