{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba3a8c51e661148e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n3\ttitle: MaaS 3.4 GA baseline changeability investigation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# MaaS 3.4 GA baseline changeability investigation\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves three strategy assumptions marked \"Needs validation\" about the MaaS 3.4 GA codebase as the xKS Dev Preview baseline: (1) whether the Tenant CRD is extensible in the 3.4 GA baseline so a configurable OIDC group claim path can be added, or is frozen; (2) whether maas-api can be instrumented with Prometheus metrics without conflicting with the 3.4 GA code freeze, or requires a post-3.4 patch; and (3) whether a stable or RC 3.4 build is available to use as the validation baseline. The answers determine the approach of the maas-controller and maas-api implementation work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Inspect the MaaS 3.4 GA repository and release policy to determine whether adding a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD is permitted in the baseline, or whether the CRD is frozen.\n34\t- Assess whether maas-api observability instrumentation (Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint) can be added to the 3.4 baseline or must be delivered as a post-3.4 patch (the strategy allows deferring metrics to P1 in that case).\n35\t- Confirm build availability: identify a stable or RC MaaS 3.4 build artifact (version and date) usable as the xKS validation baseline, or escalate unavailability to the MaaS PM (open question: latest date for a stable build, Summit timeline feasibility).\n36\t- Produce a findings record with a go/fallback determination for each question.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- The findings record states, with evidence from the MaaS 3.4 repository and release policy, whether the Tenant CRD `groupClaimPath` addition is possible in the baseline or must fall back to documenting the required claim format.\n41\t- The findings record states whether maas-api metrics instrumentation can land in the baseline or requires a post-3.4 patch (or deferral).\n42\t- A stable or RC MaaS 3.4 build artifact is identified (version/date) as the validation baseline, or the unavailability and its timeline impact is escalated and documented.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Enables HLR [P0]: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (determines code-change vs documentation-fallback approach).\n47\t- Enables HLR [P0]: Observability metrics functional (determines instrumentation approach).\n48\t\n49\t## Notes\n50\t\n51\tThe stable-build timing question is owned by the MaaS PM per the strategy's open questions table; the technical questions are answerable from the MaaS source repository and build artifacts.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"58ad9922-49dd-4087-8b7c-490dabbb7a42","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:11.457Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba3a8c51e661148e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
