{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a8bc66107927b4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n3\ttitle: 'maas-api: xKS adaptation, external OIDC configuration, metrics instrumentation,\n4\t  Helm charts'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n6\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n7\tteam: MaaS\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If maas-api observability instrumentation conflicts with the\n16\t    MaaS 3.4 GA freeze, deliver metrics as a post-3.4 patch or defer to P1 with PM\n17\t    sign-off.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# maas-api: xKS adaptation, external OIDC configuration, metrics instrumentation, Helm charts\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic adapts maas-api (and the payload-processing BBR ext_proc server) for non-OpenShift Kubernetes: external OIDC authentication configuration replacing OpenShift's KubernetesTokenReview identity, removal of OpenShift-specific assumptions (cert-manager TLS instead of OpenShift service-CA, configurable gateway class), Prometheus metrics instrumentation for the observability value proposition, and Helm chart packaging for Helm-only xKS installation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Update the MaaS AuthPolicy deployment configuration to use Authorino's `oidc` identity source with the customer's OIDC issuer URL and JWKS endpoint, driven by the existing Tenant CRD OIDC fields (`oidcIssuerURL`, `oidcClientID`, `oidcAudience`) — a configuration change, not an identity-model change.\n44\t- Confirm the API key authentication flow (`sk-oai-*`, maas-api callback validation via Authorino HTTP callback) remains functional and OIDC-agnostic; no changes expected.\n45\t- Remove OpenShift-specific assumptions in deployment configuration: cert-manager-issued TLS certificates instead of OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates; configurable gateway class name.\n46\t- Add Prometheus metrics instrumentation to maas-api (`/metrics` endpoint): token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle (creation, validation, revocation), and inference request latency, exposed as Prometheus-compatible endpoints.\n47\t- Package maas-api and payload-processing as Helm charts with configurable values for: gateway class name, OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience, group claim path), TLS certificate source (cert-manager), and PostgreSQL connection (shared with other RHAII components or dedicated — decision captured as a chart value).\n48\t- Optional mitigation (team decision, not required by HLRs): in-memory LRU cache (TTL 5 min) for validated API key hashes to tolerate PostgreSQL unavailability.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given the maas-api and payload-processing Helm charts, when rendered with the enumerated configurable values (gateway class name, OIDC issuer URL / client ID / audience / group claim path, cert-manager TLS certificate source, PostgreSQL connection), then the rendered manifests deploy maas-api and payload-processing with the Authorino `oidc` identity source driven by the Tenant CRD OIDC fields, cert-manager-issued TLS certificates, and the configured gateway class, measured by `helm template` output inspection against the enumerated values.\n53\t- Given the rendered deployment configuration, when the API key authentication path is inspected, then the maas-api callback validation (`/internal/v1/api-keys/validate`) for `sk-oai-*` API keys remains wired and independent of the OIDC identity source, measured by inspection of the rendered AuthPolicy and chart configuration (runtime behavior on a deployed instance is validated in the CKS deployment validation epic, not here).\n54\t- Prometheus metrics are exposed by maas-api including `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}` (instrumentation; dashboard integration is validated separately).\n55\t- RHOAI MaaS GA behavior is unchanged where xKS configuration is not in effect (additive/config-driven backwards compatibility).\n56\t- If maas-api instrumentation conflicts with the MaaS 3.4 GA freeze (per the baseline changeability investigation), the metrics are delivered as a post-3.4 patch or deferred with PM sign-off, and that outcome is documented.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated for user identity.\n61\t- HLR [P0]: API key authentication (`sk-oai-*` flow) functional on xKS.\n62\t- HLR [P0]: Observability metrics functional — instrumentation portion (token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events).\n63\t\n64\t## Risks\n65\t\n66\t- Observability instrumentation may require a post-3.4 patch if maas-api is frozen (strategy assumption \"Needs validation\"); approach determined by the baseline changeability investigation.\n67\t- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is pending human review per the strategy's prerequisites table.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"77d39a50-9f82-494c-9b73-c7af8a2c8baa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:15.595Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a8bc66107927b4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
