KS-specific findings and limitations, feeding the known-limitations documentation.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given an AKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and a Gateway API implementation installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n47\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n48\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and the configurable claim path set to match that format, when a user with group membership authenticates, then the user is mapped to the appropriate subscription tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n49\t- A validation report exists documenting AKS-specific findings, the GatewayClass option used, and any AKS-specific limitations versus the CKS deployment.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR [P0]: MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (RFE acceptance criterion: \"AKS AND CKS\").\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"87e798da-264f-40b2-8c3f-9e576ecfd01e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:19.321Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0903c8010316083","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
