{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80ce44d757fba2a7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n3\ttitle: 'MaaS observability: Perses dashboards and CKS Prometheus integration'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Monitoring\n6\tteam: MaaS / xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# MaaS observability: Perses dashboards and CKS Prometheus integration\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the metrics portion of the observability value proposition (P0 per the Staff Engineer Input quoted in the strategy): Perses dashboards for MaaS metrics and integration of maas-api metrics endpoints with the CKS Prometheus instance. Metrics instrumentation in maas-api is delivered separately; this epic makes those metrics visible and queryable on xKS.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Deploy Perses dashboards for MaaS on xKS, displaying token usage per user/subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, API key lifecycle metrics (creation, validation, revocation), and inference request latency.\n40\t- Configure the CKS Prometheus instance to scrape the maas-api `/metrics` endpoint (scrape targets confirmed accessible during CKS validation).\n41\t- Define Prometheus datasources for the dashboards backed by the CKS Prometheus instance.\n42\t- Verify the named metrics emitted by maas-api (`maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`) are queryable on the CKS Prometheus instance.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the CKS Prometheus instance.\n47\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Perses dashboards installed, when an admin navigates to the MaaS observability dashboard, then the dashboard displays token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours, measured by dashboard rendering with live data.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR [P0]: Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (dashboards and Prometheus integration portion).\n52\t\n53\t## Notes\n54\t\n55\tJoint ownership with the xKS Platform team per the strategy's affected components table (\"MaaS / xKS Platform\"); the xKS Platform team contributes the CKS Prometheus integration.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"193e1080-b16e-4c5a-8380-109b0fb00012","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:23.428Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80ce44d757fba2a7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
