{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a13c89fcba38b5cb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E009\n3\ttitle: 'MaaS observability: structured logging and CKS Loki integration'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Monitoring\n6\tteam: MaaS / xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# MaaS observability: structured logging and CKS Loki integration\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers the logging portion of the observability value proposition (P1 per the Staff Engineer Input quoted in the strategy): structured JSON logs for authentication decisions, rate limit enforcement, and API key validation, integrated with CKS Grafana Loki for aggregation and querying.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Emit structured JSON logs from maas-api for API key validation events (method, decision, reason).\n39\t- Configure structured logging for Authorino authentication decisions and Limitador rate limit enforcement events (including 429 responses with exceeded quota), per the strategy's affected components table.\n40\t- Format log entries for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki with label filters, using the log aggregation accessibility confirmed during CKS validation.\n41\t- Include subscription selection decisions in the structured log output.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n46\t- Given a user exceeding a configured rate limit, when the enforcement decision is made, then a structured log entry for the rate limit enforcement (429 response, exceeded quota) is retrievable from CKS Grafana Loki, measured by querying with label filters.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR [P1]: Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input).\n51\t\n52\t## Notes\n53\t\n54\tJoint ownership with the xKS Platform team per the strategy's affected components table (\"MaaS / xKS Platform\"); the xKS Platform team contributes the CKS Loki integration. Authorino/Limitador structured logging configuration is guided by the RHCL/OpenShift team per the impacted teams table.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"3e01814f-0ff3-454b-889c-cdb5a113b826","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:23.486Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a13c89fcba38b5cb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
