n by authenticated users, use for inference, independence from the OIDC provider.\n50\t   - What users must do: provide their own identity provider (OIDC-compatible), per the strategy.\n51\t\n52\t2. **Known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA** (new doc topic):\n53\t   - Operator integration excluded (Helm-based installation only).\n54\t   - Dashboard/UI integration excluded from Dev Preview.\n55\t   - Dev Preview = functional demonstration, not production-ready.\n56\t   - Limitations and engineering deltas documented during the CKS and AKS deployment validations.\n57\t   - Scope reductions from RHOAI MaaS 3.4 GA per the strategy's inclusion/exclusion table.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A published document describes the user identity flow for xKS deployments, covering OIDC provider integration, group claim to tier mapping, and API key lifecycle.\n62\t- A published document lists all known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA, incorporating the findings from both platform deployment validations.\n63\t- Both documents are technically reviewed against the implemented MaaS on xKS behavior (review sign-off recorded).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR [P1]: Known limitations documented.\n68\t- HLR [P2]: User identity flow documented for xKS deployments.\n69\t\n70\t## Notes\n71\t\n72\tDocumentation Support is \"Pending human review\" in the strategy's prerequisites table; the docs-authoring routing assumes the Red Hat docs content process is available. Priority is P0 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority `Blocker`).\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"8328b3f9-06cf-471c-b884-b22a098564bd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:27.729Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3ee5b966c6f412b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}