{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afc888837b084b7d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts (branch A)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If official RHCL Helm charts are not viable for xKS, deploy standalone\n16\t    Authorino + Limitador via upstream Helm (branch B).\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 0\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Kuadrant on xKS via official RHCL Helm charts (branch A)\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis branch epic deploys Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on non-OpenShift Kubernetes using official RHCL Helm charts, the strategy's primary deployment option, selected when the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation confirms official RHCL xKS support with Helm-based distribution. It delivers a functioning authentication and rate-limiting enforcement layer for MaaS on xKS, prioritizing CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service with Istio) per the Staff Engineer Input quoted in the strategy.\n38\t\n39\tBoundary: this epic productizes and validates the deployment mechanism itself — the isolated Kuadrant install, its configuration, and its standalone enforcement behavior. It does not repeat the gating investigation's minimal feasibility demonstration, and it does not validate the integrated MaaS stack: the CKS deployment validation epic consumes this deployment and performs the end-to-end validation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Install RHCL/Kuadrant on a CKS test cluster via the official RHCL Helm charts, configured for the Istio GatewayClass.\n44\t- Configure Authorino to use the external OIDC identity source (replacing OpenShift's KubernetesTokenReview) with the customer's OIDC issuer URL and JWKS endpoint, aligned with the MaaS AuthPolicy configuration.\n45\t- Confirm Limitador's TokenRateLimitPolicy functionality on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (no code changes expected — it works on any Kubernetes).\n46\t- Enable structured logging for authentication decisions (Authorino) and rate limit enforcement (Limitador), formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki.\n47\t- Document the RHCL chart installation and configuration procedure for reuse on AKS (envoy-gateway / azure-application-gateway GatewayClass options).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) is installed via official RHCL Helm charts on a CKS cluster and all pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks.\n52\t- Authorino validates an OIDC JWT against the configured external identity provider and rejects invalid tokens, measured by authenticated and rejected test requests.\n53\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n54\t- Structured log entries for authentication decisions and rate limit enforcement are emitted and retrievable from the CKS log aggregation, measured by querying Grafana Loki with label filters.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (Limitador deployment and enforcement).\n59\t- HLR [P0]: RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (mechanism realization).\n60\t\n61\t## Gate Conditions\n62\t\n63\tExecuted only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome A (official RHCL Helm charts viable). If outcome A does not hold, this epic is replaced by the standalone Authorino + Limitador deployment branch.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"9b9fd17c-aaea-4db8-a627-e8e74837974a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:31.806Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afc888837b084b7d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
