{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8125651b04c57c4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-C-E005\n3\ttitle: Auth enforcement via direct Envoy ext_authz integration (branch C)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If no auth enforcement path is viable on xKS, escalate to product\n16\t    leadership to re-scope the MaaS xKS Dev Preview.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 0\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Auth enforcement via direct Envoy ext_authz integration (branch C)\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis branch epic implements the strategy's contingency: when neither official RHCL Helm charts nor standalone Kuadrant deployment is viable on xKS, integrate authentication and rate-limiting enforcement directly at the gateway via Envoy's ext_authz mechanism, bypassing Kuadrant. This is a deeper architectural change that may require reworking how MaaS wires its AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy enforcement into the gateway data plane.\n38\t\n39\tBoundary: this epic implements and validates the enforcement mechanism itself — the ext_authz path and its standalone enforcement behavior. It does not repeat the gating investigation's minimal feasibility demonstration, and it does not validate the integrated MaaS stack: the CKS deployment validation epic consumes this enforcement path and performs the end-to-end validation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Design and implement Envoy ext_authz-based authentication enforcement for the MaaS gateway on xKS, validating OIDC JWTs (external identity provider) and MaaS API keys (`sk-oai-*` validation callback path).\n44\t- Implement rate-limiting enforcement equivalent to the MaaS token rate limiting tiers at the gateway or an equivalent enforcement point.\n45\t- Rework the MaaS gateway configuration (Istio GatewayClass on CKS) to route authentication and rate-limit decisions through the ext_authz path instead of Kuadrant-generated policies.\n46\t- Preserve the MaaS failure-mode behavior: API key validation remains independent of the OIDC provider; rate-limiting unavailability denies requests with HTTP 503.\n47\t- Document the architectural deviation from the Kuadrant-based design and its long-term viability implications for product leadership.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- An inference request with a valid OIDC JWT or valid MaaS API key is allowed, and a request with invalid credentials is rejected, measured by response status codes through the gateway.\n52\t- Given a configured token rate limit, when a user exceeds the limit, then requests are rejected with HTTP 429, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n53\t- Given the rate-limiting enforcement point is unavailable, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503, measured by response status and gateway logs.\n54\t- A design document describes the ext_authz-based enforcement architecture and its deviations from the Kuadrant-based MaaS architecture, reviewed by the MaaS team.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR [P0]: Token rate limiting functional on xKS (enforcement via the contingency path).\n59\t- HLR [P0]: External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (validation via the contingency path).\n60\t\n61\t## Gate Conditions\n62\t\n63\tExecuted only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS support investigation selects outcome C (no viable Kuadrant deployment on xKS). If no auth enforcement path is viable at all, the MaaS xKS Dev Preview scope must be re-negotiated with product leadership.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db71cbfae171a7a","agent_id":"a73443dcac864ec72","session_id":"1e4ce44d-83b4-4c13-8abf-b56141fd026a","uuid":"6f795c98-695a-4bbb-93e1-b9868ed7016a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:23:33.278Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8125651b04c57c4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
